Z||000000||V8Fiero||07-06-2001||10:41 PM||||OK. I know that more people than me have done this. This was really F-ing stupid of me.<P>Just got my GT running and have been driving and testing it now for the last couple of days. I took my plates off my other car until I could find the time to get to the DMV. Was gonna go on Tues. but decided to go golfing instead. (very nice day out).<P>Well today on the way back from lunch, I took a different route that I usually dont like because there is a grey area on the speed limit. It goes from 25 to 40 and isnt posted very well.<P><BR>To make a long story shorter I got nailed by the cops....BIG TIME!!!<P>41mph in a 25mph<BR>Falsifications of Registration<BR>No proof of liability insurance. (My card didnt match the car)<P>Lets run down the fines, shall we:<P>Speeding: $17<BR>Falsification of Registration: $300<BR>No liability Insurance: $300<BR>Bonded out: $60<P>They didnt impound my car. After I got out I got to tow it back home. Needless to say I have already been to the DMV, called the insurance company and got it insured.<P>Lesson Learned. That $98 dollars that it took to get it registered sure beat the hell out of the $600 + on all the other crap.<P>Got court on next friday.<P>So Please......<P>DONT BE A DUMB ASS!!!<BR><P>------------------<BR>86 SE Gold<BR>86 GT Red <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/RedRavensig.JPG"> <BR>"Trying to change from V8Fiero to RedRavenGT"||||reg||8
Z||000001||Urchin||07-06-2001||10:49 PM||||Ouch!!  Thats rough.   A friend of mine got nailed a while back for similar things.  I don't remember the specifics, but I remember him telling me that he had to got to court and could face upto $5000 in charges.  Oh ya, that's what it was...he was driving with plates from his other car, no insurance, a few other things too.  They really burn ya.||||reg||1
Z||000002||CoolBlue87GT||07-06-2001||11:10 PM||||Oh boy ! I know how you feel. Sorry to hear that happened.<P>I did something dumb today also. I got out of my car, and wanting to hear the rest of the song on the radio, I left the keys in the ignition, I went around to the other door to pick up my brief case.<P>Then after picking it up, proceeded to close the door. Only then, did I realize, AW CRAP, the keys are now locked in the car !!<P>A quick call to the local police, and an officer responding with a slim jim got me fixed up.<P>I'm now going to get that extra key made !||||reg||6
